menu "OpenTail CORE Alpha"
  config OPENTAIL_AP_PASSWORD
    string "Bench-only Wi-Fi AP WPA2 password (8-63 characters)"
    default "OpenTailLab-ChangeMe"
    help
      Change before bench testing. Do not connect this alpha unit to a vehicle.
  config OPENTAIL_BUFFER_PIXELS_PER_OUTPUT
    int "Per-output maximum pixel buffer allocation (hardware memory budget)"
    range 1 8192
    default 2048
    help
      Independent of vehicle/bench layouts. This build-time upper bound
      budgets CORE frame memory for each physical channel and prevents
      oversized profiles from exhausting an ESP32-S3. Users configure the
      actual active pixel count for each output in Output Manager; the
      RMT driver transmits only that configured count. Larger installations
      may select another budget or a different board backend after
      measuring RAM, DMA, output throughput and power. It is not an
      advertised optical FPS or tested hardware maximum.
endmenu
